{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-gen-48-1","title":"Genesis 48:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Joseph with his sons visits his sick father. 2 Jacob strengthens himself to bless them. 3 He repeats God's promise. 5 He takes Ephraim and Manasseh as his own sons. 7 He tells Joseph of his mother's grave. 8 He blesses Ephraim and Manasseh. 17 He prefers the younger before the elder. 21 He prophesies their return to Canaan.</p>\n<p>thy father. Joh 11:3 his two sons. 41:50-52; 46:20; 50:23; Job 42:16; Ps 128:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-2","title":"Genesis 48:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>strengthened. De 3:28; 1Sa 23:16; Ne 2:18; Ps 41:3; Pr 23:15; Eph 6:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-3","title":"Genesis 48:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>God. 17:1; 28:3; 35:11; Ex 6:3; Re 21:11 appeared. 28:12-19; 35:6,7,9,11,12; Ho 12:4 Luz. Jud 1:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-4","title":"Genesis 48:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Behold I. 12:2; 13:15,16; 22:17; 26:4; 28:3,13-15; 32:12; 35:11; 46:3; 47:27 Ex 1:7,11 will give. De 32:8; Am 9:14,15 everlasting. 17:8,13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-5","title":"Genesis 48:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>two sons. 41:50-52; 46:20; Jos 13:7; 14:4; 16:1-17:18 are mine. Le 20:26; Nu 1:10,32-35; 26:28-37; Isa 43:1; Eze 16:8; Mal 3:17 2Co 6:18; Eph 1:5 Reuben. 1Ch 5:1,2; Re 7:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-6","title":"Genesis 48:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>and shall be called. Jos 14:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-7","title":"Genesis 48:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Padan. 25:20 Rachel. 35:9,16-19; 1Sa 10:2; Mt 2:18 to Ephrath. Ru 1:2; 1Sa 1:1; 17:12; Mic 5:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-9","title":"Genesis 48:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>my sons. 30:2; 33:5; Ru 4:11-14; 1Sa 1:20,27; 2:20,21; 1Ch 25:5; 26:4,5 Ps 127:3; Isa 8:18; 56:3-5 bless them. 27:4,28,29,34-40; 28:3,4; 49:28; De 33:1; Heb 11:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-10","title":"Genesis 48:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>the eyes. 27:1; 1Sa 3:2; 4:15 dim. Heb. heavy. Isa 6:10; 59:1 kissed. 27:27; 31:55; 45:15; 1Ki 19:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-11","title":"Genesis 48:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>I had not. 37:33,35; 42:36; 45:26 God. Eph 3:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-12","title":"Genesis 48:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>he bowed himself.Joseph thus shewed that his external greatness did not render him forgetful of the respect due to his father. The Egyptians were remarkable for the reverence paid to old age: \"for if a young person meet his senior, he instantly turns aside to make way for him; if an aged person enter an apartment, the youth always rise from their seats;\" and Mr. Savary observes, that the same reverence is still paid to old age in Egypt.</p>\n<p>18:2; 19:1; 23:7; 33:3; 42:6; Ex 20:12; 34:8; Le 19:3,32; 1Ki 2:19 2Ki 4:37; Pr 31:28; Eph 6:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-14","title":"Genesis 48:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>his right hand. Ex 15:6; Ps 110:1; 118:16 and laid. Nu 8:10,18; De 34:9; Mt 19:13,15; 6:5; 16:18; Lu 4:40; 13:13; Ac 6:6 Ac 8:17-19; 13:3; 1Ti 4:14; 5:22 guiding. 19 firstborn. 18; 41:51; 46:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-15","title":"Genesis 48:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>blessed. 16; 27:4; 28:3; 49:28; De 33:1; Heb 11:21 did walk. 5:22-24; 6:9; 17:1; 24:20; 1Ki 3:6; Ps 16:8; Isa 30:21; Jer 8:2 Lu 1:6; 1Co 10:31; 2Co 1:12; Col 2:6; 1Th 2:12 fed me. 28:20,22; Ps 23:1; 37:3; 103:4,5; Ec 2:24,25; 5:12,18; 6:7 Isa 33:16; Mt 6:25-34; 1Ti 6:6-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-16","title":"Genesis 48:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Angel. 16:7-13; 28:15; 31:11-13; Ex 3:2-6; 23:20,21; Jud 2:1-4; 6:21-24 Jud 13:21,22; Ps 34:7,22; 121:7; Isa 47:4; 63:9; Ho 12:4,5; Mal 3:1 Ac 7:30-35; 1Co 10:4,9 redeemed. Ps 34:2; Mt 6:13; Joh 17:15; Ro 8:23; 2Ti 4:18; Tit 2:14 my name. 5; 32:28; De 28:10; 2Ch 7:14; Jer 14:9; Am 9:12; Ac 15:17 grow into. Heb. as fishes do increase. 1:21,22; Nu 1:46; 26:34,37 Fish are the most prolific of all animals: a tench lays 1,000 eggs, a carp 20,000, and Leuwenhoek counted in a middling sized cod, 9,384,000.</p>\n<p>a multitude. 49:22; Ex 1:7; Nu 26:28-37; De 33:17; Jos 17:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-17","title":"Genesis 48:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>laid his. 14 displeased him. Heb. was evil in his eyes. 28:8; 38:10; Nu 11:1; 22:34; *marg: 1Sa 16:7; 1Ki 16:25; 1Ch 21:7; Pr 24:18; Ro 9:7,8,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-18","title":"Genesis 48:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Not so. 19:18; Ex 10:11; Mt 25:9; Ac 10:14; 11:8 for this. 27:15; 29:26; 43:33; 49:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-19","title":"Genesis 48:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>said, I know it. 14; 17:20,21; 25:28; Nu 1:33-35; 2:19-21; De 33:17; Isa 7:17 Eze 27:10; Re 7:6,8 become. De 1:10; Ru 4:11,12 multitude. Heb. fulness.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-20","title":"Genesis 48:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Israel bless. 24:60; 28:3; Ru 4:11,12 and he set. Nu 2:18-21; 7:48,54; 10:22,23; 13:8,11,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-21","title":"Genesis 48:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>Behold. 50:24; 1Ki 2:2-4; Ps 146:3,4; Zec 1:5,6; Lu 2:29; Ac 13:36; 2Ti 4:6 Heb 7:3,8,23-25; 2Pe 1:14 God. 15:14; 28:15; 46:4; De 1:1-46; 31:8; Jos 1:5,9; 3:7; 23:14; 24:1-33 Ps 18:46 land. 12:5; 26:3; 37:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gen-48-22","title":"Genesis 48:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GEN","chapterStart":48,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":48,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>given. 33:19; De 21:17; Jos 24:32; 1Ch 5:2; Eze 47:13; Joh 4:5 Amorite. 15:16; 34:28; Jos 17:14-18; Jud 11:23; Am 2:9</p>"}]}